  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0])\n    \n    for c1 in range(1, 10):\n        for top in range(H):\n            for bottom in range(top + 2, H):\n                for left in range(W):\n                    for right in range(left + 2, W):\n                        # check if the border is composed entirely of color c1\n                        is_box = True\n                        for r in range(top, bottom + 1):\n                            if grid[r][left] != c1 or grid[r][right] != c1:\n                                is_box = False\n                                break\n                        if not is_box:\n                            continue\n                            \n                        for c in range(left, right + 1):\n                            if grid[top][c] != c1 or grid[bottom][c] != c1:\n                                is_box = False\n                                break\n                        if not is_box:\n                            continue\n                        \n                        # check the interior colors\n                        inside_colors = set()\n                        for r in range(top + 1, bottom):\n                            for c in range(left + 1, right):\n                                val = grid[r][c]\n                                if val != 0:\n                                    inside_colors.add(val)\n                        \n                        # the valid box must contain exactly one non-zero color different from c1\n                        if len(inside_colors) == 1:\n                            c2 = list(inside_colors)[0]\n                            if c2 == c1:\n                                continue\n                            \n                            # construct the output grid\n                            out_h = bottom - top + 1\n                            out_w = right - left + 1\n                            out_grid = [[0] * out_w for _ in range(out_h)]\n                            \n                            for i in range(out_h):\n                                for j in range(out_w):\n                                    if i == 0 or i == out_h - 1 or j == 0 or j == out_w - 1:\n                                        out_grid[i][j] = c2\n                                    else:\n                                        if grid[top + i][left + j] == c2:\n                                            out_grid[i][j] = c2\n                                            \n                            return out_grid\n                            \n    return grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0])\n    \n    for c1 in range(1, 10):\n        for top in range(H):\n            for bottom in range(top + 2, H):\n                for left in range(W):\n                    for right in range(left + 2, W):\n                        # check if the border is composed entirely of color c1\n                        is_box = True\n                        for r in range(top, bottom + 1):\n                            if grid[r][left] != c1 or grid[r][right] != c1:\n                                is_box = False\n                                break\n                        if not is_box:\n                            continue\n                            \n                        for c in range(left, right + 1):\n                            if grid[top][c] != c1 or grid[bottom][c] != c1:\n                                is_box = False\n                                break\n                        if not is_box:\n                            continue\n                        \n                        # check the interior colors\n                        inside_colors = set()\n                        for r in range(top + 1, bottom):\n                            for c in range(left + 1, right):\n                                val = grid[r][c]\n                                if val != 0:\n                                    inside_colors.add(val)\n                        \n                        # the valid box must contain exactly one non-zero color different from c1\n                        if len(inside_colors) == 1:\n                            c2 = list(inside_colors)[0]\n                            if c2 == c1:\n                                continue\n                            \n                            # construct the output grid\n                            out_h = bottom - top + 1\n                            out_w = right - left + 1\n                            out_grid = [[0] * out_w for _ in range(out_h)]\n                            \n                            for i in range(out_h):\n                                for j in range(out_w):\n                                    if i == 0 or i == out_h - 1 or j == 0 or j == out_w - 1:\n                                        out_grid[i][j] = c2\n                                    else:\n                                        if grid[top + i][left + j] == c2:\n                                            out_grid[i][j] = c2\n                                            \n                            return out_grid\n                            \n    return grid",
